+    string = s.sign("foo")
 
 .. code-block:: python
 
@@ -21,6 +21,29 @@ than a given age.
       ...
     itsdangerous.exc.SignatureExpired: Signature age 15 > 5 seconds
 
+For the higher-level :class:`TimedSerializer` (and
+:class:`.URLSafeTimedSerializer`) you can set a ``default_max_age``
+once at construction time so that every :meth:`~TimedSerializer.loads`
+call enforces the limit without having to repeat it:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from itsdangerous import TimedSerializer
+    s = TimedSerializer("secret-key", default_max_age=3600)
+    token = s.dumps({"user_id": 42})
+
+    # Works within one hour; raises SignatureExpired if older.
+    data = s.loads(token)
+
+    # Callers can still override the limit per call with an integer.
+    data = s.loads(token, max_age=7200)
+
+``default_max_age`` uses **None-falls-through** semantics: both an omitted
+``max_age`` and an explicit ``max_age=None`` resolve to
+:attr:`~TimedSerializer.default_max_age`. If ``default_max_age`` is ``None``
+(the default), no age limit is applied at all, preserving full backward
+compatibility with existing applications.
+
 .. autoclass:: TimestampSigner
     :members:
 
